---
import ZetaLayout from "../../../layouts/ZetaLayout.astro";
---
<ZetaLayout
	lang="en"
	title="Ecosystem — Zeta"
	description="Zeta's own capabilities and upstream sources: project tracking, the Web workbench, experiment measurement, command marketplace, plugin platform; upstream roles and acknowledgments — OMP mainline, Pi, OMP Web, Pi Web."
	active="ecosystem"
>
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="kicker">Ecosystem</div>
		<h1>What Zeta brings itself.</h1>
		<p class="lede">Zeta ships its own product surface on top of the OMP runtime, while keeping every upstream role publicly labeled. This page lists Zeta's own capabilities first, then the four source projects, their roles, and acknowledgments.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block" id="own">
		<div class="section-head">
			<div class="num">01</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Zeta's own capabilities</h2>
				<div class="sub">On top of the shared runtime, these are developed and maintained by Zeta itself.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="grid-table">
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">01</div><h3>Project tracking /tracking</h3><p>Milestones and key decisions written to <code class="keycap">.zeta/tracking/</code>, kept across sessions with persisted compaction summaries; off by default, explicit opt-in.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">02</div><h3>Web workbench &amp; desktop</h3><p>43 light/dark themes, trajectory view, the right-side dock, and the trusted desktop open bridge; one durable session shared with the CLI.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">03</div><h3>Experiment measurement</h3><p>Per-project local experiment tracking: metrics, directions, and baseline commits in SQLite.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">04</div><h3>TypeScript commands &amp; marketplace</h3><p>arktype / typebox / zod argument schemas; commands installed, shared, and reused as Bun packages.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">05</div><h3>IM channels &amp; multi-workspace</h3><p>WeChat / Feishu / Telegram bots, workspace aliases, and relay delegation — sessions stay in sync with the CLI and desktop.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">06</div><h3>Plugin platform</h3><p><code class="keycap">plugins/official</code> and <code class="keycap">plugins/community</code> directory structure, with the plugins manager shipped.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">07</div><h3>Remote access security</h3><p>Gateway binds loopback only by default; <code class="keycap">remote.token</code> auth with CSRF and clickjacking protection.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">08</div><h3>Local stats dashboard</h3><p><code class="keycap">zeta stats</code> local observability: sessions, usage, and cost.</p></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block" id="sources">
		<div class="section-head">
			<div class="num">02</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Reference projects</h2>
				<div class="sub">The four sources Zeta is built on.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="sources">
			<a class="source" href="https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<div>
					<div class="sname">Oh My Pi <span class="badge main">MAINLINE</span></div>
					<div class="sdesc">The runtime, CLI, local tools, and sessions — Zeta's direct upstream. Runtime tree, package layout, and Bun workflow follow OMP so updates stay mergeable.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="arrow">→</div>
			</a>
			<a class="source" href="https://github.com/earendil-works/pi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<div>
					<div class="sname">Pi <span class="badge adv">ADVANCED</span></div>
					<div class="sdesc">Semantic port source for modern agent behavior: context engineering, extension primitives, provider correctness. Ported as verifiable semantic ports, not wholesale merges.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="arrow">→</div>
			</a>
			<a class="source" href="https://github.com/17380936778/omp-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<div>
					<div class="sname">OMP Web <span class="badge main">SNAPSHOT</span></div>
					<div class="sdesc">The direct upstream of the standalone <code>web-ui/</code> snapshot: agent.db, model handling, session SSE, Windows selectors.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="arrow">→</div>
			</a>
			<a class="source" href="https://github.com/agegr/pi-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<div>
					<div class="sname">Pi Web <span class="badge adv">UX SOURCE</span></div>
					<div class="sdesc">Semantic port source for web product and UX: host whitelists, DNS-rebinding protection, CSP, project trust.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="arrow">→</div>
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block" id="research">
		<div class="section-head">
			<div class="num">03</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Research references</h2>
				<div class="sub">Studied for semantics; not merged as runtimes.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="grid-table">
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">01</div><h3>DeepSeek Reasonix</h3><p>Cache behavior research: system-prompt stability, cache diagnostics, cache-aware compaction.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">02</div><h3>OpenCode</h3><p>Model metadata, protocol semantics, and cache-handling boundaries for research only.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">03</div><h3>OpenTUI</h3><p>TUI design and interaction patterns for reference layouts, keybindings, and components.</p></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block" id="credits">
		<div class="section-head">
			<div class="num">04</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Acknowledgments</h2>
				<div class="sub">Zeta would not exist without these projects and their maintainers.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="grid-table">
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">01</div><h3>can1357</h3><p>Author and maintainer of Oh My Pi — Zeta's runtime and mainline upstream.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">02</div><h3>mariozechner / earendil-works</h3><p>Author and maintainers of Pi — source of Zeta's advanced agent behavior.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">03</div><h3>17380936778</h3><p>Maintainer of the OMP Web snapshot that seeds Zeta's <code>web-ui/</code>.</p></div>
			<div class="grid-item"><div class="idx">04</div><h3>agegr</h3><p>Author of Pi Web — source of Zeta's web security and reliability patterns.</p></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block" id="distro">
		<div class="section-head">
			<div class="num">05</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Distribution promise</h2>
				<div class="sub">Zeta is an OMP downstream distribution: runtime tree, package layout, Bun workflow, and internal <span class="keycap">@zeta/*</span> names follow OMP so upstream updates remain mergeable.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="sources">
			<a class="source" href="https://github.com/Linxira-OS/linxira-zeta" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<div><div class="sname">linxira-zeta</div><div class="sdesc">The product repository: tracking OMP upstream with continuous integration; docs and releases live here.</div></div>
				<div class="arrow">→</div>
			</a>
			<a class="source" href="https://github.com/Linxira-OS" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<div><div class="sname">Linxira-OS organization</div><div class="sdesc">The organization home: distributions and related infrastructure.</div></div>
				<div class="arrow">→</div>
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</ZetaLayout>
